"answer": "The emails regarding Q2 budget revisions highlight two main adjustments. First, Oliver Grant reports that capital expenditure projects (new office building and IT infrastructure upgrade) exceeded their budgets by 10%, necessitating a reallocation of funds and adjustments to financial projections. Second, Karen Smith outlines a revised Q2 budget and profit forecast, shifting funds toward emerging market bonds for better returns. This revision has increased the Q2 profit forecast to $9.378 million, representing a 3.5% increase from previous estimates. Additionally, Diana Wells notes that these recent budget revisions will be a focus of the upcoming Q2 financial audit."
